he is gonna go into yet.

00:02:10.042 --> 00:02:12.170
- He said, "You know what,
which one do I wanna pick?"

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:13.650
- He's gonna weigh his options.

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:14.890
- [Kelly] I love that.
- Yeah.

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:15.940
- So wait, I didn't know this,

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:17.692
but you started out as a music teacher.

00:02:17.692 --> 00:02:18.525
- I did.

00:02:18.525 --> 00:02:19.358
- I had no clue.

00:02:19.358 --> 00:02:20.191
Was it elementary?

00:02:20.191 --> 00:02:21.024
Is that what it was?

00:02:21.024 --> 00:02:21.857
- Kindergarten through six

00:02:21.857 --> 00:02:23.760
in the St. Louis Public School System.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:25.000
- [Kelly] Wow!
- Yes.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.350
- So is this so you could,

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:28.100
I imagine this is a day job.

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:30.560
Then on the weekends you did, you gigged?

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:32.390
- I did. I was in a cover band

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:34.540
and then I got in a
band as a backup singer.

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:36.150
And then I started getting commercials,

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:37.930
like a guy walked in who was a producer

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:41.070
