a McDonald's commercial,

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:44.020
which paid me twice what I'd
made in two years of teaching.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.260
- Which is such a statement for teachers.

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:48.600
I know it is, it is.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.297
It's like sometimes I look
at paychecks and I'm like,

00:02:50.297 --> 00:02:52.761
"Gosh! My mom worked so hard."

00:02:52.761 --> 00:02:54.960
- Yes. Yeah.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:58.350
- But, in the end I started
getting more commercial work

00:02:58.350 --> 00:02:59.913
and I went to LA and thought,

00:03:00.873 --> 00:03:04.010
" I'll get a record
deal and become famous."

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:05.730
- Like so many, like in your life.

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:06.810
It happened though, thank you.

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:08.070
'Cause it worked out for us too

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:08.903
that got to learn.

00:03:08.903 --> 00:03:10.170
- It was all overnight too.

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:11.003
- It was?

00:03:11.003 --> 00:03:12.610
