00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:51.534
As you get wiser,
hopefully some of us don't.

00:04:51.534 --> 00:04:52.757
- Yes, yeah.

00:04:52.757 --> 00:04:56.220
When you get to be my age,
you're gonna be really wise.

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:58.040
- No, it's like, no I do.

00:04:58.040 --> 00:04:59.600
I feel like life does get better.

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:01.350
It gets simpler and you realize like,

00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:03.670
no isn't a crappy thing to say to someone.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:04.880
It's actually just setting a boundary.

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:06.610
It's nice, I've been to therapy.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:08.410
- I love that, I love that.

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:10.197
'Cause it took me getting
breast cancer to learn,

00:05:10.197 --> 00:05:11.780
"Okay, sometimes you have to say no

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:13.300
as an exercise."
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:14.560
- You cannot make everybody happy.

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:16.743
You can't say yes to everything.

00:05:16.743 --> 00:05:17.576
- What is it with artists?

00:05:17.576 --> 00:05:18.620
Why do we, we're people pleaser.

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:19.770
- It's like in women.

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:21.772
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- So yeah.

00:05:21.772 --> 00:05:24.360
- Her new Showtime documentary
is called "Sheryl".

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:26.400
So what was it like to
look back at your life

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:27.660
and your career and this documentary,

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.400
was kind of scary or weird?

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.470
- I think for me,

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:33.900
obviously I have like 30
years of my own career

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:36.270
and then I had a whole life before that.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:37.250
I think people forget,

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:38.510
especially with social media and stuff

00:05:38.510 --> 00:05:39.970
that we're people.
- Yeah.

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:42.739
- And that behind the artistry

00:05:42.739 --> 00:05:45.000
and the drive to be an artist,

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:46.920
there's a world of challenges in there

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:50.620
that made you want to reveal
your your vulnerabilities

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:51.540
and write music.

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:54.370
And we're really quick to
judge and quick, you know?

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:56.683
So when Showtime came to me and said,

00:05:56.683 --> 00:05:57.670
" Do you wanna do documentary?"

00:05:57.670 --> 00:06:00.660
I was like, "Absolutely not."
- Yeah.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.730
- And then I kind of warmed up to the idea

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:04.430
of telling the story about the person

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:07.880
as opposed to the person
that wrote "All I wanna do"

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:10.020
and "Suck up the sun" and--

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:11.660
- 'Cause those are
different chapters of us.

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:13.100
- They are, and your big hits

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:15.810
don't necessarily represent who you are.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:17.250
They give you an opportunity to go

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:18.880
out into the world and play your songs.

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:21.470
But it's the deep cuts
that really tell the story.

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:24.260
So it's been an interesting
thing and I hope people

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:26.307
when they watch it feel
inspired and they feel like,

00:06:26.307 --> 00:06:27.140
"Oh! Okay, yeah.

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:28.230
I've gone through depression

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:31.640
or I've had sexual harassment in my life

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:35.640
or I'm getting old and what
does that mean in my career?"

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:36.700
You know, that kind of thing.
- Yeah.

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:38.860
- There's all kinds of
challenges that we all go through

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:40.170
whether you're famous or you're not.

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:41.559
So, and that's what it's about.

00:06:41.559 --> 00:06:42.392
- I agree.

00:06:42.392 --> 00:06:43.225
Was there anything,

00:06:43.225 --> 00:06:44.810
because this happens to me sometimes.

00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:46.180
It's only 20 years for me,

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:47.520
but I just mean it happens to where

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:49.557
somebody will say
something and I'll be like,

00:06:49.557 --> 00:06:50.540
"Oh my God!"

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:52.280
Was there anything like in the documentary

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:54.550
that you were like you surprised you

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:56.090
