that facial expression,"

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:44.070
you know mouth people.
- You're known for your mouth.

00:07:44.070 --> 00:07:45.360
People love your mouth.
- Oh that's very nice.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:47.015
- Like that's that's so funny.

00:07:47.015 --> 00:07:48.003
- You do?
- You're like known for it.

00:07:48.003 --> 00:07:50.480
Did you know?
- Oh my God! I love that.

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:51.600
- No, but you're known.

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:52.850
That's like one of your things.

00:07:52.850 --> 00:07:54.370
So see, this is why, okay.

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:55.810
So I don't watch,
- You can't watch yourself.

00:07:55.810 --> 00:07:56.650
- I don't watch myself.

00:07:56.650 --> 00:07:58.250
I don't watch interviews,
I don't watch any,

00:07:58.250 --> 00:07:59.300
I don't watch myself.

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:01.360
I don't or any articles
that people review,

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:02.193
anything like that.
- [Amy] Good.

00:08:02.193 --> 00:08:04.060
- Because I think it changes you.

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:06.560
And I think the things
that people love about you,

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:08.700
you'll change them and
that's what people love.

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:09.533
So do you do that?

00:08:09.533 --> 00:08:10.700
Do you read anything?
- I don't.

00:08:10.700 --> 00:08:14.900
Since my second record, I've
not read one single thing.

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:15.733
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:08:15.733 --> 00:08:17.090
- I don't want people to tell me.

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:20.520
I like being there, feel good about it

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:23.260
and then I don't want
somebody to rob me of that

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:24.610
by telling me that it wasn't good.

00:08:24.610 --> 00:08:25.584
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- And sometimes I'll be like,

00:08:25.584 --> 00:08:26.980
"That wasn't very good."

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:28.140
But I'll own that.

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:29.010
I just don't want somebody else

00:08:29.010 --> 00:08:30.563
telling me their opinion, you know?

00:08:30.563 --> 00:08:31.630
(Kelly laughs)

00:08:31.630 --> 00:08:32.837
- Stay on your own front porch, sir.

00:08:32.837 --> 00:08:34.607
- Yeah, who are you, exactly.

00:08:34.607 --> 00:08:35.670
Who asked you?

00:08:35.670 --> 00:08:36.860
So, I love that with this,

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:39.950
this was so smart because as a super fan,

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:42.090
like you also released
a greatest hits, right?

00:08:42.090 --> 00:08:42.923
With the documentary?

00:08:42.923 --> 00:08:43.756
- Yeah.
- [Kelly] With "Sheryl".

00:08:43.756 --> 00:08:46.100
So like what, tell us about that.

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:48.509
- So there's, there's obviously,

00:08:48.509 --> 00:08:52.480
the catalog is filled
with songs that are from,

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:53.390
that everybody knows.

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:54.780
And then there's some
songs that were featured

00:08:54.780 --> 00:08:57.260
in the documentary and there
then there's three new songs.

00:08:57.260 --> 00:09:01.630
And what was kind of
interesting about the new songs?

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:02.463
Well, first and foremost,

00:09:02.463 --> 00:09:04.710
there's a cover of "Rolling Stone"

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:06.300
song called "Live with me"

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:07.420
which is featured in the documentary.

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:08.290
It's the first time I ever got to sing

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:09.730
with "The Rolling Stones".
- Wow!

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:10.840
- And I was super nervous.

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:13.407
But we recut it and then I thought,

00:09:13.407 --> 00:09:16.340
"I'm just gonna text Sir. Mick Jagger.

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:18.140
I have his phone number, Oh my God!"

00:09:18.140 --> 00:09:18.973
- [Kelly] That's amazing.

00:09:18.973 --> 00:09:21.040
- And asked him if he
played some harmonica on it

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:22.190
and he's like, "Yeah."

00:09:22.190 --> 00:09:23.050
And so I sent it

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:24.620
and so he's on it.
- Wow!

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:28.240
- And then I don't ever put
my kids in social media.

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:29.077
I never have.
- Yeah.

00:09:29.077 --> 00:09:32.480
- And they're actually
featured in the video

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:33.313
called "Forever".

00:09:33.313 --> 00:09:35.980
And I wrote it really for my kids

00:09:35.980 --> 00:09:38.720
just 'cause our kids now are so stressed

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:41.260
and they have big things they live with.

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:42.330
I mean, we're in a war.

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:45.780
Are we gonna lose somebody
that we love to a pandemic?

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:47.140
I mean, there's all these.
- And just growing up.

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:48.347
- Not to mention being a teenager.

00:09:48.347 --> 00:09:49.537
- Those are hard times.

00:09:49.537 --> 00:09:50.630
- And social media.

00:09:50.630 --> 00:09:52.090
And so I wrote a song called "Forever"

00:09:52.090 --> 00:09:54.207
and they're featured in
that and they're just,

00:09:54.207 --> 00:09:56.130
- [Kelly] I love that.
- Rashes.

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:58.140
- And one day he's gonna
play bass with you,

00:09:58.140 --> 00:09:59.240
it's my favorite part.
- One day he's gonna play bass

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:00.073
with me.

00:10:00.073 --> 00:10:01.210
- Oh! Like that would kill.

00:10:01.210 --> 00:10:02.170
I would cry.

00:10:02.170 --> 00:10:03.981
- I just feel certain,

00:10:03.981 --> 00:10:06.420
by the time he gets to be old
enough to be in his own band

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:08.810
that being in his mom's band
is probably not gonna be

00:10:08.810 --> 00:10:10.040
like a cool thing.
- I think he's gonna be rad

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:10.873
and he can do both.

00:10:10.873 --> 00:10:12.280
He can do both.
- Yeah. Maybe.

00:10:12.280 --> 00:10:13.220
- Yeah. I'm just saying

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:15.000
- He's probably gonna ask
me though right off the bat

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:18.042
like what he's gonna make,
you know what I mean,

00:10:18.042 --> 00:10:18.875
like, "What's my salary?"

00:10:18.875 --> 00:10:19.708
- But you know what,
you've raised him right.

00:10:19.708 --> 00:10:21.120
- That's right.
- "I know my worth, mom."

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:22.430
- That's right, business man.

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:24.370
- So wait, so your
lyrics, they're very pure.

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:25.520
They're very raw and honest.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:28.310
That's what I gravitated
towards and still do.

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:29.940
So what's your writing process?

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:31.490
Like it's always different for all of us.

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:32.970
Like I have to be completely alone.

00:10:32.970 --> 00:10:33.950
Like what's yours?

00:10:33.950 --> 00:10:36.650
- Yeah. Well I went through
years where it was like

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:37.690
I gotta be tortured,

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:40.150
I have to have at least seven
or eight bottles of wine

00:10:40.150 --> 00:10:41.078
by myself.

00:10:41.078 --> 00:10:41.911
(Kelly laughs)

00:10:41.911 --> 00:10:44.753
And then I can only have between
11 and six in the morning.

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:47.120
And after breast cancer,

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:50.600
I felt like I had this
three-month-old baby.

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:53.137
I brought him home the second he was born.

00:10:53.137 --> 00:10:55.300
And the world looked
different to me, you know?

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:57.330
And I found that I could write,

00:10:57.330 --> 00:10:59.460
if I could just sit down quietly

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:01.520
and I'm a big meditator as well.

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:02.600
If I could just like--
- You're good at that?

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:03.650
I need to be good at that.

00:11:03.650 --> 00:11:05.723
- Well, it's a practice.
- I know.

00:11:05.723 --> 00:11:07.626
- It's not a perfect,

00:11:07.626 --> 00:11:08.960
it's a practice.
- I know, okay.

00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:09.820
- And that's so cliche.

00:11:09.820 --> 00:11:11.710
But yeah, I mean that helps too.

00:11:11.710 --> 00:11:15.350
So I just find that creativity is not,

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:17.960
you can't just schedule it in,

00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:21.530
but you can be awake and enough
to get outta your own way.

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:24.240
Sometimes I craft a song
'cause I know how to do it.

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:26.980
Other times, something just,
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:28.337
- Like the song "Forever" I go,

00:11:28.337 --> 00:11:30.670
"Where did that come from?"

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:32.597
- That's my favorite
time when you're like,

00:11:32.597 --> 00:11:34.765
"Okay, so I was just purely
the vessel for that."

00:11:34.765 --> 00:11:35.598
- [Amy] Yes.

00:11:35.598 --> 00:11:36.642
- Like I love that moment
and it just flows outta you.

00:11:36.642 --> 00:11:38.500
- You're just like, "Thank you."

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:39.740
- And you can't believe you did something,

00:11:39.740 --> 00:11:41.850
you're like "Cool."
- Yes, yeah.

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:43.380
- 'Cause most of the
time it's not like that.

00:11:43.380 --> 00:11:45.590
It's rare I feel like from, maybe not you.

00:11:45.590 --> 00:11:48.290
- Show up and you're like, "No, it is."

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:50.300
I made a record called "Be myself"

00:11:50.300 --> 00:11:53.650
and we made it in three
weeks and I was so inspired,

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:54.560
worked with my buddy Jeff

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:59.130
and we made it between school
drop off and school pickup.

00:11:59.130 --> 00:12:01.540
And it was the most
fun record I ever made.

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:02.774
- Oh my God! That should
have been the title.

00:12:02.774 --> 00:12:04.130
- Nobody bought it and nobody heard it,

00:12:04.130 --> 00:12:05.150
- That should have been the title.

00:12:05.150 --> 00:12:05.983
- But it was so great.

00:12:05.983 --> 00:12:07.007
- "School drop off, School pickup".

00:12:07.007 --> 00:12:09.057
- Yes! That's exactly.

00:12:09.057 --> 00:12:10.473
"Drop off, pickup".

